1
00:00:00,920 --> 00:00:02,000
[ANNE]
Mr. Collins!

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:03,580
[ORLAND]
Daana, please fetch a doctor!

3
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,960
- [DAANA] Yes, sir!
- [KING] Stay calm, Elliott!

4
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:07,880
[NADIR]
What do we do? He's bleeding!

5
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,960
[VALENTINE] Press some cloth
against the wound!

6
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,500
♪

7
00:01:45,790 --> 00:01:47,710
- [Elliott groans]
- Mister Collins!

8
00:01:47,790 --> 00:01:48,750
Are you awake?

9
00:01:48,830 --> 00:01:52,790
[groans]

10
00:01:53,750 --> 00:01:56,670
[ELLIOTT]
It would seem that I survived.

11
00:01:57,290 --> 00:01:59,960
Bridget, I'm happy you're here
to see me, too!

12
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:03,080
Am I to assume
that you helped tend to me?

13
00:02:03,170 --> 00:02:04,420
Uh!

14
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,380
[inhales]

15
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:06,630
Never mind, then.

16
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:08,540
[ANNE]
Good news!

17
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:10,750
Seems Mister Collins
is all right!

18
00:02:10,830 --> 00:02:12,790
I wasn't really invested,
either way.

19
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:13,920
Well, that's rude.

20
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,830
You could at least pretend
like you were worried,

21
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:18,500
- even if you weren't.
- [CHALLE] You could but not me.

22
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:20,460
More importantly,
I have a question.

23
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:21,710
Who did this to you?

24
00:02:21,790 --> 00:02:22,790
Mm?

25
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:23,960
I haven't a clue.

26
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:25,080
He was wearing a hood

27
00:02:25,170 --> 00:02:26,790
and it all happened
very suddenly.

28
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:28,080
Were you robbed?

29
00:02:28,170 --> 00:02:29,250
Oddly, no.

30
00:02:29,330 --> 00:02:31,630
He said he could smell
silver sugar on me

31
00:02:31,710 --> 00:02:34,290
and asked if I was
a silver sugar master.

32
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:35,500
When I said that I wasn't,

33
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:37,290
he started slashing away at me.

34
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:40,460
Do you know something, Challe?

35
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:44,210
- [gasps]
- You're a warrior fairy?

36
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:46,170
Why didn't anyone tell me
about that?

37
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:47,250
[sword swings]

38
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,630
[CHALLE] Did the blade resemble
this one?

39
00:02:50,830 --> 00:02:53,630
Hm. The shimmer on the blade
did look like that

40
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:56,000
but I don't believe
the metal was silver.

41
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:58,670
I heard a sound, like a blade
slicing through wind,

42
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:00,880
and saw a flash of light,
almost red.

43
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:02,210
[CHALLE]
I see.

44
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,580
There is no question,

45
00:03:05,670 --> 00:03:07,420
the one who assaulted him
was a fairy.

46
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:09,830
[gasps] You're saying
that someone sent a fairy

47
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:11,630
to attack Mister Collins?

48
00:03:11,710 --> 00:03:12,670
[CHALLE]
Perhaps so.

49
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:14,920
That's terrible.
Why would anyone--

50
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
[CHALLE]
I don't know.

51
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:17,250
That's fine.

52
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:19,170
I survived the ordeal
in one piece,

53
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:21,750
so the who and why of it
doesn't matter much right now.

54
00:03:22,630 --> 00:03:24,290
You needn't worry about me.

55
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:25,210
Go.

56
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:27,330
There's important business
to attend to.

57
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:28,290
Huh?

58
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:30,710
The selection is coming soon.

59
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:33,420
Mister Glen didn't make
the decision to enter lightly.

60
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:35,790
You owe it to him
to produce a good result.

61
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:37,750
[distant birds chirp]

62
00:03:37,830 --> 00:03:39,710
[GLEN]
Elliott said that to you?

63
00:03:39,790 --> 00:03:40,750
Yes.

64
00:03:40,830 --> 00:03:44,000
Fortunately, it seems
his injuries aren't too serious.

65
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:46,040
Hmm, he's truly grown

66
00:03:46,130 --> 00:03:48,420
into a fine young gentleman,
hasn't he?

67
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:52,040
I trust him
to take good care of Bridget.

68
00:03:52,130 --> 00:03:55,330
I'd be at peace, if only I could
put the matter to rest.

69
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:56,670
[sighs]

70
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:58,000
Forgive me.

71
00:03:58,080 --> 00:03:59,540
I'm just speaking my mind,

72
00:03:59,630 --> 00:04:01,290
I know
there's nothing you can do.

73
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:02,750
[ANNE]
It's all right.

74
00:04:02,830 --> 00:04:06,210
Well, as Elliott said,
you have an important job to do.

75
00:04:06,290 --> 00:04:08,630
Uphold the good reputation
of our shop.

76
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:09,880
Yes, sir.

77
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:11,290
We'll make you proud.

78
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:16,630
♪

79
00:04:21,790 --> 00:04:23,750
Now, shall we begin?

80
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:25,880
You said
we're making snow, correct?

81
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:27,790
But snow has no form.

82
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:29,460
How will we even express it?

83
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:30,750
It's simple.

84
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:32,290
I'll draw it for you.

85
00:04:35,670 --> 00:04:36,880
This is snow!

86
00:04:37,670 --> 00:04:40,420
Try making whatever shape
of crystal comes to mind!

87
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,330
[ALL]
Hm.

88
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,380
[ANNE]
These are all lovely

89
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:49,790
and I think it's good
that there are different sizes.

90
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:53,250
But since it's snow,
it should be piled up.

91
00:04:53,330 --> 00:04:55,000
A tower might be good!

92
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,830
Oh, yes! I agree!

93
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,080
That's perfect!

94
00:04:58,170 --> 00:04:59,630
We should make it transparent.

95
00:04:59,710 --> 00:05:00,920
It will make for a good effect

96
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,920
if the light in the room
passes through it.

97
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,710
In that case, I think
we should add a bit of color.

98
00:05:05,790 --> 00:05:07,630
That'll be striking
when the light hits it.

99
00:05:07,710 --> 00:05:09,080
We should adjust the kneading.

100
00:05:09,170 --> 00:05:11,040
So, let's increase
the number of folds.

101
00:05:11,130 --> 00:05:12,210
It'll be more glossy.

102
00:05:12,290 --> 00:05:13,290
Mm-hm.

103
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:14,830
The base will be pure white.

104
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:17,380
We'll accent it
with the palest blue and pink,

105
00:05:17,460 --> 00:05:19,000
a hint of purple, too.

106
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:20,500
We'll need to make lots.

107
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:22,750
And how much is "lots," exactly?

108
00:05:22,830 --> 00:05:24,750
As many as we can, for now.

109
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:27,580
We're aiming to impress,
so bigger is better, right?

110
00:05:27,670 --> 00:05:29,750
We should have plenty,
if we all work hard.

111
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:31,420
I have faith in your skills.

112
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:32,960
So, let's start now!

113
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:38,630
♪

114
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:15,880
[crickets chirp]

115
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:21,000
We're happy?

116
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:22,710
[all gasp]

117
00:06:22,790 --> 00:06:24,000
No complaints.

118
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:25,080
Looks good.

119
00:06:25,170 --> 00:06:26,170
[door opens]

120
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:27,630
I brought him to see!

121
00:06:27,710 --> 00:06:28,630
Hello!

122
00:06:28,710 --> 00:06:30,330
I heard you finished the, uh--

123
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:32,210
[gasps]

124
00:06:33,210 --> 00:06:34,250
Goodness.

125
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:37,920
This is amazing.

126
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,040
♪

127
00:06:48,290 --> 00:06:49,170
Ah?

128
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:51,170
[ORLAND]
Mister Glen!

129
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:53,540
I can't stay in bed
at a time like this.

130
00:06:53,630 --> 00:06:55,000
I have to see your work.

131
00:06:55,710 --> 00:06:57,750
[running footsteps]

132
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,540
[GLEN]
It's snow.

133
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:05,500
[exhales]

134
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:07,580
A snowy landscape.

135
00:07:08,710 --> 00:07:11,080
Lovely, it would be a dream

136
00:07:11,170 --> 00:07:12,920
to see
Saint Lewiston Bell Church

137
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,380
lined with these!

138
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:18,130
Anne, come here please.

139
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:20,920
You're the Head of Artisans,
aren't you?

140
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,000
[Anne gasps]

141
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:25,500
[GLEN] What? You said it
yourself, if I recall.

142
00:07:26,540 --> 00:07:27,500
Ah!

143
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:31,460
This is wonderful work
you've done.

144
00:07:33,170 --> 00:07:35,330
Anne, go to Lewiston Bell,

145
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:37,500
to represent
the Paige school's workshop

146
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:39,170
as our Head of Artisans.

147
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:40,830
Yes, sir!

148
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:43,460
Challe, you accompany her.

149
00:07:43,540 --> 00:07:45,290
Whoever it was
that attacked Elliott

150
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:47,080
may target one of you again.

151
00:07:47,170 --> 00:07:50,040
I've heard rumors that
people are after silver sugar.

152
00:07:50,130 --> 00:07:52,500
Ensure that Anne reaches
the church safely.

153
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:53,540
Understood?

154
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:55,500
I will obey your orders.

155
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:58,750
- [birds chirp]
- [wagon rattles]

156
00:08:02,290 --> 00:08:04,040
[ELLIOTT]
The sun will set before long.

157
00:08:04,130 --> 00:08:06,630
What should we do now,
warrior fairy?

158
00:08:06,710 --> 00:08:08,880
We will continue
to Lewiston just like this.

159
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:10,420
Visibility should be fine.

160
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:11,630
It's a full moon.

161
00:08:11,710 --> 00:08:13,000
But we're prepared to camp,

162
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:14,710
you're sure
we should go all night?

163
00:08:15,330 --> 00:08:16,580
It's to avoid the fairy.

164
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:20,080
He's attracted by the scent
of silver sugar.

165
00:08:20,170 --> 00:08:21,880
[CHALLE]
So, we need to keep moving.

166
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:24,790
If we go far enough,
we may be able to elude him.

167
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,750
♪

168
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:34,830
Now that we've traveled
this far,

169
00:08:34,920 --> 00:08:36,210
perhaps we'll be safe.

170
00:08:36,290 --> 00:08:37,670
[wind howls]

171
00:08:37,750 --> 00:08:39,380
[Anne gasps]

172
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:43,960
[exhales]

173
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,580
[gasps]

174
00:08:47,670 --> 00:08:49,000
That would be him.

175
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,960
♪

176
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,170
Careful.

177
00:09:01,250 --> 00:09:02,580
[Challe cloths patter]

178
00:09:03,790 --> 00:09:05,040
[CHALLE]
I'll keep him busy.

179
00:09:05,830 --> 00:09:08,170
While I do that, keep moving.

180
00:09:08,250 --> 00:09:10,630
Go, I can catch up with you.

181
00:09:10,710 --> 00:09:11,540
[horse neighs]

182
00:09:11,630 --> 00:09:13,630
♪

183
00:09:14,170 --> 00:09:16,420
[swords clink]

184
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:17,750
Come back safe!

185
00:09:17,830 --> 00:09:19,960
[grunts]

186
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:25,540
[MITHRIL]
Don't worry, Anne.

187
00:09:25,630 --> 00:09:26,670
He'll be fine.

188
00:09:26,750 --> 00:09:27,750
You should trust him.

189
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:29,250
I do.

190
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:33,670
- [HOODED FAIRY] Obsidian, is it?
- Hm?

191
00:09:34,250 --> 00:09:37,000
I haven't seen a fellow
precious stone in a while.

192
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:38,580
I don't want to fight you.

193
00:09:38,670 --> 00:09:40,750
I would much rather save you.

194
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:42,920
Which one among them
holds your wing?

195
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:44,420
[CHALLE]
You first.

196
00:09:45,330 --> 00:09:47,130
Who and where is your master?

197
00:09:47,210 --> 00:09:48,290
[Hooded Fairy chuckles]

198
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:51,580
My wings are mine
and mine alone.

199
00:09:51,670 --> 00:09:53,210
[CHALLE]
You're saying you're free, then.

200
00:09:53,830 --> 00:09:54,880
[chuckles]

201
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:57,830
But being alone
can be rather inconvenient.

202
00:09:58,170 --> 00:10:00,960
I wouldn't mind
having at least one ally.

203
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:04,040
♪

204
00:10:04,420 --> 00:10:06,250
Allow me to set you free.

205
00:10:06,330 --> 00:10:07,670
I'll chase down your captors

206
00:10:07,750 --> 00:10:09,460
and retrieve your wing
from them.

207
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:11,380
While I'm at it,
I'll kill them all

208
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:13,250
and steal that sugar confection.

209
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:16,130
[CHALLE]
You want sugar confections?

210
00:10:16,210 --> 00:10:19,330
I do and a silver sugar master
as well.

211
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:21,710
Do they happen to have a master
in their group?

212
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:25,420
[CHALLE]
Ah. I understand now.

213
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:29,420
I cannot give you the things
that you desire,

214
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:30,630
not a one!

215
00:10:30,710 --> 00:10:31,540
[Challe grunts]

216
00:10:31,630 --> 00:10:33,960
This after I said
that I would set you free?

217
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:36,380
I already have someone
fighting to save me.

218
00:10:36,460 --> 00:10:38,170
So, I have no need of you.

219
00:10:38,250 --> 00:10:39,580
Intriguing.

220
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:44,790
We're not going fast enough,
Orland, hurry up!

221
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:47,040
We can't!
The sugar confection will break!

222
00:10:47,130 --> 00:10:49,000
Perhaps, but if that bandit
catches up to us--

223
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:50,290
That won't happen!

224
00:10:50,380 --> 00:10:51,920
Have faith in Challe's plan.

225
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,380
He won't let that fairy
get one step closer!

226
00:10:56,670 --> 00:10:58,380
[NADIR]
It's Lewiston!

227
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:01,080
[MARCUS]
Don't rush!

228
00:11:01,170 --> 00:11:02,710
Unload it carefully.

229
00:11:02,790 --> 00:11:04,170
[ELLIOTT]
We've just arrived!

230
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:06,250
We're from the main Paige
workshop!

231
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,750
I'm here on behalf
of Glen Paige.

232
00:11:08,830 --> 00:11:10,460
My name is Elliott Collins.

233
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:12,330
We have brought
a sugar confection.

234
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:14,210
We're entering the selection.

235
00:11:14,290 --> 00:11:16,460
[BROOK] Well, well.
Please come this way.

236
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:17,750
Bring your sugar confection--

237
00:11:17,830 --> 00:11:18,920
- What is the meaning of this?
- [ELLIOTT] Good,

238
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:19,920
- let's get started!
- He said

239
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,540
they wouldn't be participating!

240
00:11:22,670 --> 00:11:26,040
♪

241
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:30,670
[BROOK] It is time to begin
this year's selection process.

242
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:32,460
The participants are:

243
00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:35,170
the main workshop
of the Radcliffe school,

244
00:11:35,250 --> 00:11:37,540
the main workshop
of the Mercury school,

245
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:40,170
and the main workshop
of the Paige school.

246
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:43,540
Hm?

247
00:11:43,630 --> 00:11:45,580
[BROOK]
First, the Radcliffe Workshop.

248
00:11:45,670 --> 00:11:46,710
Go ahead.

249
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:50,500
Ah.

250
00:11:51,130 --> 00:11:52,460
Hm.

251
00:11:54,330 --> 00:11:56,380
[priests impressed]

252
00:11:56,460 --> 00:11:59,170
- [PRIEST 1] Oh, splendid.
- [PRIEST 2] Very impressive

253
00:11:59,790 --> 00:12:03,000
[ANNE] It looks like Challe.
It must be Keith's work.

254
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,750
[MARCUS]
Our theme is the founding king,

255
00:12:04,830 --> 00:12:06,960
whose various depictions
and achievements

256
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:08,500
will be represented.

257
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:10,830
This piece is
but one such example.

258
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:13,960
We envision a number of them
standing in rows in the church.

259
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:17,460
- [PRIEST 3] I see.
- [PRIEST 4] How ambitious.

260
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:19,420
[BROOK]
Next, the Mercury Workshop.

261
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:20,670
If you would.

262
00:12:20,750 --> 00:12:22,460
[JOHN]
We will create 12 spheres,

263
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:25,000
each with one of
the Twelve Patron Saints within,

264
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:26,920
as you see here.

265
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,790
The pieces would line the church
on each side.

266
00:12:30,710 --> 00:12:32,630
[BROOK]
And finally, the Paige Workshop.

267
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:33,630
Go ahead.

268
00:12:33,710 --> 00:12:35,170
[exhales]

269
00:12:36,330 --> 00:12:37,330
Huh?

270
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:38,920
[exhales]

271
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,420
Huh?

272
00:12:47,580 --> 00:12:48,630
Hm.

273
00:12:55,290 --> 00:12:58,080
The theme of our confection
is snow.

274
00:13:01,330 --> 00:13:04,000
[indistinct chatter]

275
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:09,630
[ANNE] It's completely different
from how it looked

276
00:13:09,710 --> 00:13:12,040
in the workshop, but why?

277
00:13:12,130 --> 00:13:14,670
[BROOK] Is something wrong?
Please continue.

278
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:18,920
[ANNE]
These are snow crystals.

279
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:22,750
The way it cleanses the soul
represents Holy Beginnings.

280
00:13:22,830 --> 00:13:24,460
[grunts]

281
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:26,290
[ANNE] When visitors come
to the church,

282
00:13:26,670 --> 00:13:28,000
our piece will...

283
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:30,290
This is terrible.

284
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:31,750
[ANNE]
Everything's wrong.

285
00:13:31,830 --> 00:13:33,080
What should I do?

286
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:35,750
[door opens]

287
00:13:36,830 --> 00:13:40,710
♪

288
00:13:41,790 --> 00:13:42,920
[gasps]

289
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:44,580
[ANNE]
Challe.

290
00:13:52,330 --> 00:13:53,630
[ANNE]
Light!

291
00:13:53,710 --> 00:13:54,670
Oh!

292
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:56,130
One moment, Father.

293
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:58,040
Could we cast some light
on our piece?

294
00:13:58,130 --> 00:13:59,040
I want you to see it

295
00:13:59,130 --> 00:14:01,710
as it would look
in the Holy Beginnings Festival!

296
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:07,790
♪

297
00:14:16,750 --> 00:14:19,130
[all laughing]

298
00:14:19,210 --> 00:14:21,080
[giggles]

299
00:14:21,710 --> 00:14:22,920
That's quite a change!

300
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,040
[dazzling sound]

301
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:32,710
[ANNE] Once again, the theme
of our piece is "snow."

302
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:34,080
Snow falls from heaven,

303
00:14:34,170 --> 00:14:36,960
with a prayer that good fortune
will come in the new year.

304
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:39,210
It shrouds the kingdom
in pure white.

305
00:14:39,290 --> 00:14:41,290
We gave form
to those shining crystals,

306
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:42,710
which make everything new,

307
00:14:42,790 --> 00:14:45,170
and chose to depict a snowscape.

308
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:46,830
This would be one of many.

309
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:49,000
We hope to line the church
with them.

310
00:14:50,380 --> 00:14:51,630
[ANNE]
That's all.

311
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:55,000
[BROOK]
Any of these sugar confections

312
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:56,000
would be worthy of

313
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,670
- the Holy Beginnings Festival?
- The whole matter was settled.

314
00:14:57,750 --> 00:14:59,080
Let's give the fathers a moment

315
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:01,000
- to deliberate.
- This is unique.

316
00:15:01,790 --> 00:15:04,750
It seems that we've already come
to our decision.

317
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:09,000
It is quite clear
that the workshop best suited

318
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:11,420
for this
Holy Beginnings Festival

319
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:12,790
- is the Paige School...
- [gasps]

320
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:16,000
...and their beautiful
snowscape confection!

321
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:17,790
[chuckles]

322
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,250
[chuckles]

323
00:15:19,330 --> 00:15:21,630
[HEAD PRIEST 1] Artisans
of the Paige school workshop,

324
00:15:21,710 --> 00:15:24,250
we will entrust you
with the full display,

325
00:15:24,330 --> 00:15:26,830
to make this church truly shine.

326
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:29,880
Please do your best
until the end of the year,

327
00:15:29,960 --> 00:15:32,330
so we can share your vision
of hope and rebirth

328
00:15:32,420 --> 00:15:34,380
with the entire kingdom!

329
00:15:34,460 --> 00:15:35,790
[ELLIOTT]
Understood!

330
00:15:37,580 --> 00:15:39,000
[ANNE]
I can't believe it.

331
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,710
We did it!

332
00:15:40,790 --> 00:15:42,630
They chose us!

333
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,960
That went so well, I wish
I could have made this with you!

334
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:51,380
- Oh, right!
- Huh?

335
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:54,580
Anne, hold out your hand, please.

336
00:15:54,670 --> 00:15:55,670
Hm?

337
00:15:58,630 --> 00:16:00,500
What? You're sure? But why?

338
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:01,830
It's only fair.

339
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:03,630
When Mister Glen said
he'd throw you out

340
00:16:03,710 --> 00:16:05,540
if we weren't chosen,
you should have countered

341
00:16:05,630 --> 00:16:07,960
with a demand of your own,
instead of just saying yes!

342
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:09,670
If you'd been thinking
on your toes,

343
00:16:09,750 --> 00:16:11,130
you would have asked
for the wing back

344
00:16:11,210 --> 00:16:12,460
if we won the selection today.

345
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:14,000
She's not that clever!

346
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:16,420
Stop expecting the impossible
from poor Anne!

347
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:17,580
- [grunts]
- [chuckles]

348
00:16:17,670 --> 00:16:20,420
Frankly, we were feeling a bit
sorry for you... [chuckles]

349
00:16:20,500 --> 00:16:21,960
...so we made a decision.

350
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:23,670
If our workshop
was chosen today,

351
00:16:23,750 --> 00:16:25,210
we'd pay you in kind.

352
00:16:27,830 --> 00:16:29,380
I knew it right from the start,

353
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:31,210
you're just
like the first silver sugar.

354
00:16:31,290 --> 00:16:32,170
[exhales]

355
00:16:32,710 --> 00:16:34,420
You know, I keep hearing that,

356
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:36,210
but no one will explain it
to me.

357
00:16:36,290 --> 00:16:38,580
What does
"the first silver sugar" mean?

358
00:16:41,330 --> 00:16:43,540
It means
"that which brings change."

359
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:46,210
When you refine silver sugar,

360
00:16:46,290 --> 00:16:49,330
you leave sugar apples
in cold water overnight, right?

361
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:52,460
And you always have to add
a handful of silver sugar.

362
00:16:53,750 --> 00:16:57,670
In our school, that's called
"the first silver sugar."

363
00:16:57,750 --> 00:17:01,330
Without it, no matter how long
you soak the sugar apples,

364
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:04,080
their bitterness
will never go away.

365
00:17:04,170 --> 00:17:06,880
That's why the first
silver sugar is special.

366
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,210
It brings change.

367
00:17:08,290 --> 00:17:09,580
It starts something new.

368
00:17:09,670 --> 00:17:11,460
I had high hopes for you

369
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:13,920
and so I called you
that endearingly.

370
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,250
Luckily, you met
all my expectations!

371
00:17:17,330 --> 00:17:19,000
Thank you, Anne.

372
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,210
You've taught our school

373
00:17:20,290 --> 00:17:22,500
how to take
a fresh step forward.

374
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:24,750
So, I won't tie you down
any longer.

375
00:17:24,830 --> 00:17:26,830
You're free to do
as you please now.

376
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,790
[gasps]

377
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:41,460
[ANNE]
Challe? [echoing]

378
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:43,790
[CHALLE] I smell the aroma
of silver sugar.

379
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:47,630
That sweet, beloved scent.

380
00:17:47,710 --> 00:17:50,250
Like it's reaching out
to embrace me.

381
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:58,000
Ah, you're awake.

382
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:59,000
Huh?

383
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:01,710
[MITHRIL]
Is that a cut on your arm I see?

384
00:18:01,790 --> 00:18:03,080
[gasps]

385
00:18:03,170 --> 00:18:04,460
Hm.

386
00:18:05,170 --> 00:18:06,500
[ANNE]
That looks bad.

387
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:07,960
Are you all right?

388
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:08,920
[CHALLE]
Yes.

389
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:11,080
I'll heal soon.

390
00:18:11,170 --> 00:18:12,290
I see.

391
00:18:13,210 --> 00:18:14,790
And what about the fairy?

392
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:17,630
He ran away but next time,
he'll be dead.

393
00:18:17,710 --> 00:18:19,040
[exhales]

394
00:18:19,130 --> 00:18:21,670
As long as you're safe,
that's all that matters.

395
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:23,290
Thank you again, Challe.

396
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:25,290
You're always working hard
to protect me.

397
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:27,500
[CHALLE]
What's that?

398
00:18:27,580 --> 00:18:29,250
Oh, they're returning your wing.

399
00:18:29,330 --> 00:18:31,330
Since they were chosen
in the selection today,

400
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:32,960
they said I've done enough.

401
00:18:33,040 --> 00:18:35,170
I don't have to work for them
anymore if I don't want

402
00:18:35,250 --> 00:18:36,580
but then...

403
00:18:37,750 --> 00:18:38,830
Mm?

404
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:39,750
♪

405
00:18:39,830 --> 00:18:42,290
[ANNE] The real work
for the Holy Beginnings Festival

406
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:43,630
starts now.

407
00:18:43,710 --> 00:18:46,750
Is it really all right for me
to leave them alone?

408
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,830
Say, I was wondering,

409
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:53,710
if maybe I should stay
at the Paige Workshop

410
00:18:53,790 --> 00:18:55,630
until the festival is over,
at least.

411
00:18:55,710 --> 00:18:56,750
[MITHRIL]
Oh?

412
00:18:56,830 --> 00:18:58,170
It's only fair.

413
00:18:58,250 --> 00:19:00,500
I haven't fulfilled
my responsibilities.

414
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:03,790
I haven't truly rebuilt
the workshop yet.

415
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:07,670
So for now,
until this project is complete,

416
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:09,420
I want to give them my best.

417
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:12,040
Is that all right?

418
00:19:12,130 --> 00:19:13,250
[giggles]

419
00:19:13,330 --> 00:19:15,170
That sounds just lovely to me!

420
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:17,500
The bed there is
awfully comfortable, you know?

421
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:20,040
You can do whatever it is
you please.

422
00:19:20,130 --> 00:19:22,960
As long as we're together,
I'm content.

423
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:24,630
Thank you both.

424
00:19:24,710 --> 00:19:25,710
Good, then!

425
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:27,710
I'll go tell them the news
right away!

426
00:19:27,790 --> 00:19:31,170
I'm sure everyone was secretly
hoping they could keep you!

427
00:19:31,250 --> 00:19:34,170
That's a relief
and I'm glad you're happy, too!

428
00:19:36,710 --> 00:19:38,380
I'm sorry about this.

429
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:40,330
I'm just dragging you along.

430
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:42,040
[CHALLE]
It doesn't bother me.

431
00:19:42,130 --> 00:19:44,250
You're still interesting
to watch.

432
00:19:44,330 --> 00:19:46,080
Everything else is just a bore.

433
00:19:46,170 --> 00:19:47,330
[Anne chuckles]

434
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:53,420
I'm sorry
this has taken so long.

435
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:56,380
Thank you for waiting on me
to return your wing.

436
00:19:56,830 --> 00:19:58,920
This is yours alone, take it.

437
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:04,130
[chuckles softly]

438
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,000
Huh?

439
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:16,040
You saved me.

440
00:20:16,630 --> 00:20:17,540
It's done.

441
00:20:18,330 --> 00:20:21,080
You became a silver sugar master
by your own strength.

442
00:20:21,750 --> 00:20:22,960
Hold your head up high.

443
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,380
You've earned it.

444
00:20:25,460 --> 00:20:27,380
I will.

445
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:31,540
♪

446
00:20:35,170 --> 00:20:38,290
[CHALLE] To you, who have become
a silver sugar master,

447
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:39,960
I wish many blessings.

448
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:55,880
♪

